## Audius

Evaluate integration with the official Audius developer API.

Potential capabilities include:

- Track search.
- Artist profiles.
- Album and playlist discovery.
- Track metadata.
- Authorised streaming.
- Charts and discovery.

Most read-only API endpoints are available without user authentication, while higher rate limits or write operations may require authentication and API credentials.

Follow current developer documentation and API limitations.

Reference:

https://docs.audius.co/

## Jamendo

Evaluate official Jamendo API integration.

Potential features include:

- Track search.
- Artists.
- Albums.
- Playlists.
- Metadata.
- Licensed streaming.
- Creator-authorised downloading.

Respect Creative Commons licences, attribution requirements, commercial restrictions and download permissions.

Check each track's actual download availability.

Reference:

https://developer.jamendo.com/

## YouTube Music-Compatible Adapter

Treat this as an optional experimental integration.

Study the general architecture of:

- InnerTune.
- OuterTune.
- ViMusic.
- Other maintained and legally compatible community projects.

Do not blindly copy code.

Audit all external project licences before considering code reuse.

Do not request Google passwords.

Do not collect or scrape user cookies.

Do not bypass DRM, advertisements, access controls, Premium entitlements or content restrictions.

Do not introduce unauthorised audio extraction or offline downloads.

Where a compliant integration cannot provide a requested operation, clearly communicate the limitation and open the official YouTube Music application instead.

The entire SoundShelf application must remain usable if this experimental module stops working.

## Spotify Integration

Provide an optional Spotify provider or external-app integration according to permitted Spotify functionality.

Possible functionality:
- Content links.
- Track metadata where authorised.
- Artist and album references.
- Playlist metadata where permitted.
- Opening tracks in Spotify.
- Supported playback-control handoff.

Do not build an unrestricted Spotify audio-streaming client.

Do not combine Spotify streams with content from other providers where prohibited.

Respect current Premium requirements and developer-policy restrictions.

Reference:

https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/

## Provider Independence

Each provider must be independently enableable and disableable.

A failed provider must not:
- Crash SoundShelf.
- Corrupt the playback queue.
- Break local music.
- Prevent other providers from working.
- Reset playlists.
- Destroy playback history.

Provide provider status and useful error messages.

