# 11. ACCOUNT CONNECTION AND AUTHENTICATION

Account connection must be optional.

Users must never need an online account to play local music.

Provide a dedicated Connected Services screen.

For each provider, show:

- Provider name.
- Connection status.
- Available capabilities.
- Authentication method.
- Disconnect option.
- Information about provider restrictions.

Use officially supported OAuth flows where available.

Prefer Authorization Code with PKCE for public Android clients where supported by the provider.

Never ask users to type their Google or Spotify account passwords into SoundShelf.

Never store third-party passwords.

Do not collect browser cookies or authentication session tokens through unofficial means.

Store authorised tokens securely using Android Keystore-backed encryption.

Support token expiry, refresh where permitted, revocation and disconnection.

Do not store unnecessary personal account information.

Clearly distinguish:
- Connected account.
- External application installed.
- Unauthenticated browsing.
- Experimental provider.
- Unsupported playback.

