# 20. PRIVACY AND OFFLINE ARCHITECTURE

SoundShelf should be privacy-conscious and transparent about connectivity.

There must be no:
- Advertisements inserted by SoundShelf.
- Analytics SDKs.
- Advertising SDKs.
- Hidden tracking.
- Telemetry.
- Crash-report uploads.
- Mandatory accounts.
- Mandatory cloud synchronisation.
- Remote configuration unrelated to enabled providers.
- Unnecessary background network requests.

All local music functionality must work offline.

Local playlists, play counts, history, settings and metadata should be stored locally.

Online provider integrations must only use the network when the user actively accesses online functionality or an explicitly enabled provider feature requires it.

Do not transmit local music filenames or library contents to external providers without a clear, necessary and user-approved action.

Do not silently scan and upload the user's music library.

Do not upload audio files to external services for recognition.

Provide a clear privacy explanation for every connected provider.

## Two Build Variants

