# FINAL PRODUCT VISION

**SoundShelf — Your Music. Your Library. Your Experience.**

Build a beautiful, fully featured native Android music player combining local music, online music discovery, authorised streaming integrations, advanced playback, lyrics, playlists and legitimate download discovery.

Users should be able to:

- Open the application and immediately play local music.
- Discover new music online.
- Search artists, albums and songs.
- Connect compatible music services.
- Use supported streaming providers.
- Build playlists.
- Read synchronized lyrics.
- Inspect audio quality.
- Manage local music metadata.
- Find legitimate downloadable versions of recordings.
- Enjoy a sophisticated Now Playing experience.
- Personalise the application's visual identity.

Local playback must never depend on an online provider.

Streaming providers must remain modular and independently replaceable.

The application must be honest about provider restrictions, content licences, download rights and authentication capabilities.

No SoundShelf advertisements.
No trackers.
No mandatory account.
No unnecessary cloud services.
No forced subscription.
No bloated interface.

Build a complete Android application with a genuinely excellent local music experience and an expandable online music ecosystem.

**The local music player is the foundation. The streaming ecosystem is the extension. The listening experience is the product.**